+For a deliberately temporary browser task, `desktop_open_browser(url, lifetime="temporary_session")` opens a fresh owned Chromium when doctor reports the optional provider available. Its browser, profile and unsaved content are deleted on disconnect, backend close or reconnect: save outside it before ending the session. It never attaches an existing profile. Start with `desktop_inspect(window_id=..., role="entry")` to avoid browser-chrome noise, then use its distinct `text_fields` IDs with the usual read/focus/select/type tools; inspect by `name` for an intended button. Fields report `multiline` and `line_break_semantics`. Ordinary HTML text inputs and textareas need no paragraph option; native AX `nodes` remain separate. Input uses the owned browser's native text protocol, without clipboard replacement. Protected fields, unregistered rich editors, frames and shadow-root fields are unsupported. A cooperating paragraph editor supports whole-field replace or append at the end; LF requires `line_breaks="paragraph"`. Its readback distinguishes paragraph structure and actual marks. Existing text/marks are preserved when appending; formatting of newly inserted text follows the application, and whole-field replacement removes the old content. Unsupported nodes or marks are refused, not flattened. Active or unconfirmed composition is refused before focus/input; never cancel it automatically. Focus and content can race between checks and dispatch, so an uncertain error may include input delivered elsewhere: observe before retrying. A cleanup-unconfirmed error blocks another owned browser in that backend.
